Universal Scene Description (OpenUSD), originally developed by Pixar,
is a framework for interchange of 3D computer graphics data.  It
provides scene description with layering, referencing and variants for
non-destructive composition, a fast scalable runtime, schemas for
geometry, shading (UsdShade, MaterialX), lights, physics and skeletal
animation, and Hydra, a rendering architecture with the Storm
real-time renderer.

This package includes the C++ libraries, Python bindings (pxr), the
command line tools (usdcat, usdchecker, usdrecord, usdzip, ...), Hydra
Storm on Metal (macOS) or OpenGL, the Embree Hydra renderer, and
plugins for Alembic, Draco, OpenImageIO, OpenColorIO, OpenVDB, Ptex
and MaterialX.  usdview is not included.
